review_text:
Hands down my favorite restaurant in NYC. It's a mix of Afro-Caribbean cuisine that is both welcoming to those who know it well and inviting to those who don't. My recommendations are the hamachi escovitch, the egusi dumplings, the oxtail and crab rangoons, and the fried branzino. If you're on the fence about dessert, I'd skip it and opt for another cocktail instead. I've yet to try a dessert here that has blown me away. The music, which is on the loud side, is a nostalgic mix of hip-hop and R&B.  This is the ideal place for a boozy friends dinner or a swanky date, but you can also get away with bringing your parents or co -workers. If the latter, I recommend an early reservation (before 7PM) to try to avoid overlapping with a rowdy group. The music can get loud so it's not the place for a serious conversation. 

Finally, wear the dress!  Wear the heels!  This is the place to show up and show out.  

@alex.eats.365
